WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.867
On this slide, we are focusing on parameters receive values.

00:00:03.867 --> 00:00:08.597
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.597 --> 00:00:14.712
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.712 --> 00:00:18.822
A parameter is the placeholder name in the function definition.

00:00:18.822 --> 00:00:23.382
An argument is the actual value supplied when the function is called.

00:00:23.382 --> 00:00:28.647
Think about where this function would appear in a larger project.

00:00:28.647 --> 00:00:35.167
Cleaning one value, calculating one metric, or validating one record can become a reusable function applied

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.752
across many rows, files, or notebooks.

00:00:36.752 --> 00:00:42.522
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:42.522 --> 00:00:47.937
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
